      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Sir:\n\nI had splited the patch into two patches:\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/2752328 ANDROID: uid_sys_stat: split the global lock uid_lock to the fine-grained\n\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/2756209 ANDROID: uid_sys_stat: instead update_io_stats_uid instead of update_io_stats...\n\nAnd shadow-copy can only be applied for non-debug case, the reason is below:\n\nThere are three reasons to skip shadow copy for debug cases:\n\nFor debug cases, the function would register new task_entry to uid_entry so that it is necessary to hold the lock:\nupdate_io_stats_uid_locked()-\u003eadd_uid_io_stats()-\u003efind_or_register_task()\n\nComputing the data of task_entries, which it needs to alloc memory for all the task_entry and memcpy the data. It would fail to do the above operation since kmalloc(*, GFP_ATOMIC).\nupdate_io_stats_uid_locked()-\u003ecompute_io_uid_tasks()\n\n3.On the other hand it would result in high-cpuload of memcpy.",
