      "writtenOn": "2023-09-19T09:43:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are three reasons to skip shadow copy for debug cases:\n1. For debug cases, the function would register new task_entry to uid_entry so that it is necessary to hold the lock:\nupdate_io_stats_uid_locked()-\u003eadd_uid_io_stats()-\u003efind_or_register_task()\n\n2. Computing the data of task_entries, which it needs to alloc memory for all the task_entry and memcpy the data. It would fail to do the  above operation since kmalloc(*, GFP_ATOMIC).\nupdate_io_stats_uid_locked()-\u003ecompute_io_uid_tasks()\n\n3.On the other hand it would result in high-cpuload of memcpy.\n\nFor the above reasons, only shadow copy in non-debug cases.",
